  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The glass gauge on a cylindrical coffee maker shows there are \\(45\\) cups left when the coffee maker is \\(36\\%\\) full. How many cups of coffee does it hold when it is full?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(80\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(100\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(125\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(130\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(262\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "125"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1988-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(n\\) be the full capacity. Then \\(\\dfrac{45}{n} = \\dfrac{36}{100}.\\)\n\nSolving, \\(n = \\dfrac{45 \\times 100}{36} = 125\\) cups.\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Set up a proportion: \\(45\\) cups is to the full amount as \\(36\\) is to \\(100\\)",
        "If \\(36\\%\\) is \\(45\\) cups, first find how many cups \\(4\\%\\) is"
      ],
